WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.791
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:06.091 --> 00:00:09.803
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.103 --> 00:00:16.203
Unit twenty: Asking for Directions. In this unit, you will ask for and give directions in town.

4
00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:18.229
Excuse me.

5
00:00:18.929 --> 00:00:22.067
Excuse me means a polite way to get someone's attention.

6
00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:24.227
Excuse me, where is the bank?

7
00:00:24.927 --> 00:00:27.858
Your turn. Say: Excuse me.

8
00:00:30.558 --> 00:00:31.756
Excuse me.

9
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:33.565
Straight on.

10
00:00:34.265 --> 00:00:36.300
Straight on means forward without turning.

11
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.564
Go straight on for two blocks.

12
00:00:39.264 --> 00:00:41.522
Your turn. Say: Straight on.

13
00:00:44.222 --> 00:00:45.200
Straight on.

14
00:00:46.183 --> 00:00:47.150
Turn left.

15
00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.267
Turn left means change direction to the left.

16
00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:52.067
Turn left at the school.

17
00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:55.188
Your turn. Say: Turn left.

18
00:00:57.888 --> 00:00:58.749
Turn left.

19
00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:00.600
Turn right.

20
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.636
Turn right means change direction to the right.

21
00:01:03.936 --> 00:01:05.274
Turn right at the bridge.

22
00:01:05.974 --> 00:01:08.580
Your turn. Say: Turn right.

23
00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:12.293
Turn right.

24
00:01:13.283 --> 00:01:13.959
Corner.

25
00:01:14.659 --> 00:01:17.100
Corner means the place where two streets meet.

26
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.958
The shop is on the corner.

27
00:01:19.658 --> 00:01:21.962
Your turn. Say: Corner.

28
00:01:24.662 --> 00:01:25.408
Corner.

29
00:01:26.417 --> 00:01:27.650
Traffic lights.

30
00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:32.335
Traffic lights means red, yellow and green lights that control cars.

31
00:01:32.635 --> 00:01:34.681
Turn left at the traffic lights.

32
00:01:35.381 --> 00:01:38.474
Your turn. Say: Traffic lights.

33
00:01:41.174 --> 00:01:42.442
Traffic lights.

34
00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:44.161
Far.

35
00:01:44.861 --> 00:01:46.744
Far means a long way away.

36
00:01:47.044 --> 00:01:48.614
Is it far from here?

37
00:01:49.314 --> 00:01:52.164
Your turn. Say: Far.

38
00:01:54.864 --> 00:01:55.668
Far.

39
00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:57.475
Near.

40
00:01:58.175 --> 00:01:59.989
Near means not far; close.

41
00:02:00.289 --> 00:02:02.184
The museum is near the river.

42
00:02:02.884 --> 00:02:05.270
Your turn. Say: Near.

43
00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:08.750
Near.

44
00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:12.063
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:12.363 --> 00:02:15.024
Excuse me, how do I get to the museum?

46
00:02:16.317 --> 00:02:19.384
Go straight on, then turn left at the traffic lights.

47
00:02:20.683 --> 00:02:22.114
Is it far from here?

48
00:02:23.417 --> 00:02:26.382
No, it's near. About five minutes on foot.

49
00:02:27.683 --> 00:02:28.824
Is it on the right?

50
00:02:30.117 --> 00:02:32.673
It's on the corner, next to the post office.

51
00:02:33.983 --> 00:02:36.111
Grammar focus: How do I get to ?.

52
00:02:36.411 --> 00:02:39.249
How do I get to the bank? Turn right at the corner.

53
00:02:39.549 --> 00:02:42.616
Start with 'Excuse me' to be polite, and say 'Thank you' at the end.

54
00:02:43.617 --> 00:02:46.106
Now read and listen. Finding the Museum.

55
00:02:46.406 --> 00:02:50.382
A tourist stopped me and said, “Excuse me, how do I get to the museum?”

56
00:02:51.683 --> 00:02:54.867
I told her to go straight on and turn left at the traffic lights.

57
00:02:56.183 --> 00:02:58.438
The museum is on the corner, near the river.

58
00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:02.783
It isn't far, only five minutes on foot.

59
00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.805
She smiled and said, “Thank you so much!”

60
00:03:08.117 --> 00:03:10.839
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:11.139 --> 00:03:12.906
How do I get blank the museum?

62
00:03:13.206 --> 00:03:16.047
A, to. B, at. C, in.

63
00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.608
The answer is A: to.

64
00:03:23.117 --> 00:03:25.244
Red, yellow and green lights are blank.

65
00:03:25.544 --> 00:03:29.685
A, traffic lights. B, corners. C, maps.

66
00:03:33.683 --> 00:03:36.287
The answer is A: traffic lights.

67
00:03:37.783 --> 00:03:39.365
Not far means blank.

68
00:03:39.665 --> 00:03:42.808
A, near. B, far. C, straight.

69
00:03:46.817 --> 00:03:48.549
The answer is A: near.

70
00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:53.596
Now it's your turn to speak. How do you get from your house to your school?

71
00:03:58.896 --> 00:04:04.323
I go straight on along my street, then I turn right at the traffic lights. My school is on the corner.

72
00:04:04.623 --> 00:04:06.437
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:11.716
Great work today! You learned eight new words and how do i get to ?.

74
00:04:12.016 --> 00:04:15.423
Today's value is helpfulness. Help your friends and neighbours.

75
00:04:15.723 --> 00:04:18.375
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

76
00:04:18.675 --> 00:04:21.281
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

